angelings even NOTICE its effect behind a constant wave of superheroes and the occasional Dinosaur. So many Chris Pratt chimaera.....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T15:44:49-07:00","id":1096063,"title":"","content":"That may be (and we will probably need an entire other topic on &quot;Superheroes and the Dreaming&quot;), but I don't think it lessens the point of my previous post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T15:52:41-07:00","id":1096067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1095501-are-dragons-becoming-banal?p=1096063#post1096063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That may be (and we will probably need an entire other topic on &quot;Superheroes and the Dreaming&quot;), but I don't think it lessens the point of my previous post</div> </div> </div> </div>GOT is both not as big as you think it is and Changelings don't care. I mean they don't kill SPrites who just exist because of peter pan. They've had decades of Tolkien and D&amp;D to to deal with. GOT is just another in a long line of fantasy bits. I mean there's premade character in Fool's Luck who's method musing is By GMing D&amp;D and her Dreamers are her group.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T06:27:07-07:00","id":1096273,"title":"","content":"I think we're not on the same page, here.<br /> My point is not that GoT may have a strong or not strong influence on the Dreaming. But that is a &quot;cynical&quot; fantasy and therefore the Changelings in the know may not like it (because you know, superheroes stories resemble the classic fantasy way more than GoT), generally and for the eventual Glamour it inspire.<br /> <br /> (and there's that &quot;The Winter is coming&quot; catchphrase that is way too ominous, for Changelings...)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> NOTE: I'm not trying to make it a GoT Hate\\Love War, the books have their worth, I'm not trying to deny this fact","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T07:31:48-07:00","id":1096315,"title":"","content":"GoT is just one series (one very delayed series) of many fantasy series published in the past forty years. I think that the Harry Potter series, which probably still sells better than GoT, has probably had ten times the impact on the Dreaming as GoT. And its movies have probably been seen by at least ten times as many people as the GoT TV series (which is not easily accessible by the majority of humanity).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T13:57:08-07:00","id":1096471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1095501-are-dragons-becoming-banal?p=1096273#post1096273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we're not on the same page, here.<br /> My point is not that GoT may have a strong or not strong influence on the Dreaming. But that is a &quot;cynical&quot; fantasy and therefore the Changelings in the know may not like it (because you know, superheroes stories resemble the classic fantasy way more than GoT), generally and for the eventual Glamour it inspire.</div> </div> </div> </div>GRM's style isn't really all that cynical or bloody. I mean it is compared to LOTRs its probably about what your Dark Ages Vampire Elder would call &quot;Realsitic&quot; especially the Dragons and random Zombie invasions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (and there's that &quot;The Winter is coming&quot; catchphrase that is way too ominous, for Changelings...) </div> </div> </div>Or that the Dreaming is adapting to handle it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T15:35:39-07:00","id":1096506,"title":"","content":"GoT is the tenth best selling fantasy series, meaning that its individual books have sold a quarter as much as Watership Downs, a book about rabbits, so I am thinking that it effect of the Dreaming is one of many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T16:26:23-07:00","id":1096520,"title":"","content":"Given that so many of our old myths and fairy tales (and TV, film, and other fiction fills some of the same role as myths once did for the modern day) are absolutely <i>soaked</i> in blood, incest, and grotesqueries, I can't see Changelings freaking out over how Game of Thrones is poisoning glamour. The little Mermaid ends in tears and heartbreak, Red Riding Hood is brutally eaten alive in a rape metaphor, Cinderella's wonderful suitor tortures two women either to death or to where death is an enviable fate. Hercules roamed the world murdering and raping people with impunity, Zeus is basically the number one suspect for any unsolved sex crime in Classical Greece if the myths are anything to go off, and Odin tore out his own eye and was more than happy to kill anyone who crossed him. Saturn literally tore his own children apart with his teeth, half of the stories of the Dreamtime involve some kind of (usually brutal) killing, the Morrigan roams around starting wars for the sheer pleasure of it, and Osiris was torn limb from limb and cast into the damn river!<br /> <br /> Let's not forget these events actually happen in the Dreaming, as reflections of belief. So a Changeling might well remember stumbling on a version of the Norse Fimbulwinter one day - compared to that, what the fuck does he care about some muttered tagline that 'winter is coming'? He already knows Winter is coming, and he's <i>seen</i> it. Maybe the creation of an association between Winter and fantastic stories is even a good thing - maybe Frozen and Game of Thrones are an attempt by the human spirit of dreaming to fight back and make sure some glamour stays in the world as the 'real' Winter blasts into us, by exploiting the common symbolic links between fictional winter and 'real' Winter. By the same token, to the troll who's seen Odin with his own eyes up on the tree screaming in pain, blood gushing down his cheek and his body rent and battered, what does he care for some <i>pretend</i> gore that humans play with? To the Boggan who watched a contingent of noble Sidhe murder his Freehold in the Accordance War, it might even be a welcome thing to have a fantasy series out there contributing to reshaping the dreaming away from the idea that nobles are just such lovely, perfect creatures. Maybe if that idea dissolves enough, the Sidhe will lose some of their advantage.<br /> <br /> Honestly, by the dual standards of 'things that have actually happened' and 'classical myth and fairy tales prior to bowdlerization', Game of Thrones rates barely a peep of outrage. If it can pollute the Dreaming or glamour, then the Dreaming has spent many, many years in far darker places before and that's just part of life. We have this idea that fairy tales and myths are somehow cleaner, even though we know they're full of blood and gore. I wonder if a big part of why is that we learn most of those when we're children, so our internalized versions are the sanitized ones that we were given and the ones our own minds created for an inability to really understand what was taught in those myths - and if part of it also isn't that we can't <i>see</i> myths the way we see TV. We don't see, with excruciating detail, Saturn pulling off the head of a baby and feasting on its meat while great tears of horror, anguish, and rage run down his cheeks, or the way he rends his beard in grief at what he does - a sight objectively more horrifying than pretty much anything in Game of Thrones. The best we can get there is the piece by Goya.<br /> <br /> As to Dragons, why the hell would Game of Thrones make them 'banal'? The presence of the fantastic in the human mind does the exact opposite, and the Dragons in GoT are nothing less than extraordinary works of CGI with incredible screen presence, a sense of <i>realness</i> that isn't there in most depictions, and who literally represent the return of Magic to the world and the great hope against Westeros's winter. The Twilight comparison quite simply doesn't map, because the complaints about it by vampires are the same complaints as everyone else - the vampires in those books are, well, lame and somehow sexless despite being romance figures who have the sex. The complaint is 'oh god this is so dorky, is this what people think of us?' When the dragons on screen are <i>amazing</i>, that complaint just... Doesn't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","user":"loomer","date":". 05-24-2017, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T21:29:44-07:00","id":1096599,"title":"","content":"Speculative fiction keeps the Dreaming alive. I would be much more afraid of the influence of self-help books on the Dreaming. What could be more banal than Chicken Soup for the Soul or The Secret?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T22:04:45-07:00","id":1096605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1095501-are-dragons-becoming-banal?p=1096599#post1096599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speculative fiction keeps the Dreaming alive. I would be much more afraid of the influence of self-help books on the Dreaming. What could be more banal than Chicken Soup for the Soul or The Secret?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The Seven Habits of Highly Effective Dauntain</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T23:08:31-07:00","id":1096626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1095501-are-dragons-becoming-banal?p=1096599#post1096599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speculative fiction keeps the Dreaming alive. I would be much more afraid of the influence of self-help books on the Dreaming. What could be more banal than Chicken Soup for the Soul or The Secret?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They are extremely long term ravaging practices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}